window.DOCS["6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5"]={"id":"6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5","summary":{"title_zh":"關於議程項目 17 (c)：支持執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新（非正式文本）","what":"這是第二工作小組提出的非正式文本（non-paper），內容是檢討並更新「保護區工作計畫」，使其更符合綱要目標 3，並討論納入保育共生地與生態連結性的做法。多項內容（名稱、定義、生態連結性與人權做法）仍在方括號內，尚未定案。","points":["決定將工作計畫名稱修訂為更廣的用語，以反映更大的範圍，名稱用字（「保護與保育區」或「保護區及保育共生地」）仍在方括號內，尚未定案。","核可附件所列的補充活動，作為工作計畫的更新，以支持綱要的執行，特別著重目標 3（「核可」一詞仍在方括號內，尚未定案）。","鼓勵締約方與其他政府，依國情、法律與優先事項，將更新後的工作計畫納入達成綱要相關目標的行動中。","鼓勵締約方依綱要 C 節與第 8(j) 條等規定執行工作計畫，並確保原住民族與地方社區充分、公平、包容且有效地參與（是否採用以人權為基礎的做法尚未定案）。","要求執行秘書在資源許可且避免重複的前提下，進一步支持「目標 3 實踐社群」作為彈性、包容且自願參與的平臺，並邀請原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年參與。","生態連結性的處理方式尚未定案，草案提出兩個方案：設立第五個工作計畫要素，或僅作為跨領域的補充活動。"],"open":["工作計畫名稱的用字，以及「保育區」的定義是否應明確承認原住民族與傳統領地（第 2、3 段）。","生態連結性是設為工作計畫的第五個要素，還是僅作為跨領域的補充活動（第 11 段與附件第二部分）。","是否在第 12、13 段要求締約方加強生態連結性，並留待第 18 次締約方大會決定是否需要額外的生態連結性指導。","執行工作計畫時是否採用以人權為基礎的做法（第 9 段與附件第 2 段），以及是否納入原住民族自身治理制度與保護環境人權捍衛者。","是否邀請已開發國家締約方、自願承擔義務之締約方、非主權出資者（如融資機制）等動員資金（第 6、7 段，整段仍在方括號內）。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p001.md","en":[{"t":"Agenda item 17 (c)"},{"t":"Scientific and technical needs to support the implementation"},{"t":"of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"and matters related to the work programme of the"},{"t":"Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity"},{"t":"and Ecosystem Services: strategic review of and updates to"},{"t":"the programme of work on protected areas"},{"t":"Working Group II"},{"t":"Scientific and technical needs to support the implementation of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework: strategic review of"},{"t":"and update to the programme of work on protected areas"},{"t":"Non-paper"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling its decisions VII/28 of 20 February 2004, VIII/24 of 31 March 2006, IX/18 of"},{"t":"30 May 2008, X/31 of 29 October 2010, 14/8 of 29 November 2018, 15/4 of 19 December 2022 and 16/12 of 1 November 2024,"},{"t":"Acknowledging that the programme of work on protected areas1 and related decisions of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity2 continue to provide a strategic framework for the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,3 in particular Target 3, while noting that complementary activities are needed to enhance its alignment with the Framework and address identified gaps,"},{"t":"Recognizing that [ecological representativeness and] ecological connectivity [are critical qualitative requirements][is a foundational condition] for achieving ecologically representative, wellconnected, effectively conserved and managed, and equitably governed systems[ of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] under Target 3 of the Framework, and contributes to the achievement of other relevant targets and Goal A of the Framework,"},{"t":"[Noting the ongoing preparation by the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services on the methodological assessment of integrated biodiversityinclusive spatial planning and ecological connectivity, and its potential relevance for the further [development and] implementation of the programme of work,]"},{"t":"1. [Welcomes][Takes note of] the forthcoming seventh International Union for Conservation of Nature World Protected and Conserved Areas Congress, organized in Panama by the International Union for Conservation of Nature, the World Commission on Protected Areas and the Ministry of Environment of Panama;"},{"t":"[2. Adopts the definition of “conserved areas” as “areas with other effective area-based conservation measures”,4 [recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable;]]"},{"t":"3. Decides to revise the name of the programme of work on protected areas to “programme of work on [protected and conserved areas” in order to reflect the broader scope of][protected areas and [areas with] other effective area-based conservation measures[, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]”], in a manner consistent with Target 3 of the KunmingMontreal Global Biodiversity Framework, in accordance with national circumstances and legislation, and to enhance clarity and coherence;"},{"t":"1 Decision VII/28, annex."},{"t":"2 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"3 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"4 Decision 14/8, para. 2."}],"blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 17 (c)\n支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求，以及與生物多樣性及生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台工作計畫相關事項：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新\n第二工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 17 (c)<br />\n支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求，以及與生物多樣性及生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台工作計畫相關事項：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新<br />\n第二工作小組</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新\n非正式文件\n締約方大會，","html":"<p>支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求：保護區工作計畫之策略性審查與更新<br />\n非正式文件<br />\n締約方大會，</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2004 年 2 月 20 日之決議 VII/28、2006 年 3 月 31 日之決議 VIII/24、2008 年 5 月 30 日之決議 IX/18、2010 年 10 月 29 日之決議 X/31、2018 年 11 月 29 日之決議 14/8、2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/4 以及 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 16/12，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2004 年 2 月 20 日之決議 VII/28、2006 年 3 月 31 日之決議 VIII/24、2008 年 5 月 30 日之決議 IX/18、2010 年 10 月 29 日之決議 X/31、2018 年 11 月 29 日之決議 14/8、2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/4 以及 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 16/12，</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"**承認**保護區工作計畫$^1$及《生物多樣性公約》締約方相關決議$^2$持續為實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要$^3$（特別是目標 3）提供策略性框架，同時**注意到**需要補充性活動以增強其與綱要的一致性並解決已識別之差距，","html":"<p><strong>承認</strong>保護區工作計畫<sup>1</sup>及《生物多樣性公約》締約方相關決議<sup>2</sup>持續為實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>3</sup>（特別是目標 3）提供策略性框架，同時<strong>注意到</strong>需要補充性活動以增強其與綱要的一致性並解決已識別之差距，</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"**認識到**[生態代表性與]生態連結性[是關鍵的品質要求][是基礎條件]，對於在綱要目標 3 下實現具生態代表性、連結良好、受有效保育與管理，且治理公平之系統[之保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，]至關重要，並有助於達成綱要之其他相關目標與長期目標 A，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>[生態代表性與]生態連結性[是關鍵的品質要求][是基礎條件]，對於在綱要目標 3 下實現具生態代表性、連結良好、受有效保育與管理，且治理公平之系統[之保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地，]至關重要，並有助於達成綱要之其他相關目標與長期目標 A，</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"[**注意到**生物多樣性及生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台正持續進行關於整合生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估之準備工作，及其對於工作計畫進一步[開發與]實施之潛在相關性，]","html":"<p>[<strong>注意到</strong>生物多樣性及生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台正持續進行關於整合生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估之準備工作，及其對於工作計畫進一步[開發與]實施之潛在相關性，]</p>","en":[17]},{"md":"1.\n[**歡迎**][**注意到**]即將於巴拿馬由世界自然保護聯盟、世界保護區委員會及巴拿馬環境部共同舉辦之第七屆世界自然保護聯盟世界保護區與保育區大會；","html":"<p>1.<br />\n[<strong>歡迎</strong>][<strong>注意到</strong>]即將於巴拿馬由世界自然保護聯盟、世界保護區委員會及巴拿馬環境部共同舉辦之第七屆世界自然保護聯盟世界保護區與保育區大會；</p>","en":[18]},{"md":"2.\n[採納「保育區」之定義為「具有保育共生地之區域」，$^4$[在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地；]]","html":"<p>2.<br />\n[採納「保育區」之定義為「具有保育共生地之區域」，<sup>4</sup>[在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地；]]</p>","en":[19]},{"md":"3.\n**決定**將保護區工作計畫之名稱修訂為「[保護與保育區]工作計畫」，以反映[保護區與[具有]保育共生地[，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]]之更廣泛範圍」，其方式應與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 3 一致，並符合國家情況與立法，且以增強清晰度與一致性為目的；","html":"<p>3.<br />\n<strong>決定</strong>將保護區工作計畫之名稱修訂為「[保護與保育區]工作計畫」，以反映[保護區與[具有]保育共生地[，在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地]]之更廣泛範圍」，其方式應與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 3 一致，並符合國家情況與立法，且以增強清晰度與一致性為目的；</p>","en":[20]},{"md":"---\n$^1$ 決議 VII/28，附件。\n$^2$ 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^3$ 決議 15/4，附件。\n$^4$ 決議 14/8，第 2 段。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>1</sup> 決議 VII/28，附件。<br />\n<sup>2</sup> 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>3</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>4</sup> 決議 14/8，第 2 段。</p>","en":[21,22,23,24]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p002.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"4. [Endorses] the complementary activities for further or improved guidance contained in the annex to the present decision as an update to the programme of work to support the implementation of the Framework, with particular focus on Target 3;"},{"t":"5. Encourages Parties and other Governments to integrate the updated programme of work in the development and implementation of actions to meet the relevant targets of the Framework, in particular Target 3, subject to national circumstances, legislation and priorities; [6. Invites [developed country Parties, Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country] Parties, other Governments, subnational and local governments [and nonsovereign contributors, such as financing mechanisms], the private sector and philanthropic organizations, to mobilize, in accordance with Article[s] 20 [and 21] of the Convention on Biological Diversity and Target 19 of the Framework, new, additional, predictable, adequate and accessible financial resources from all sources to support the implementation of the updated programme of work, in particular for developing countries, including small island developing States, in accordance with paragraph 6 of Article 20 of the Convention;]"},{"t":"[7. Recognizes the importance of mobilizing predictable, adequate and sustainable means of implementation, including through financial resources, technical and scientific cooperation and capacity-building, to ensure the effective implementation of the updated programme of work;]"},{"t":"8. Invites the secretariats of relevant biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements, international organizations and United Nations entities, including the Global Partnership on Ecological Connectivity, indigenous peoples and local communities, including the private sector, academia, non-governmental organizations, women, youth and other relevant stakeholders, to contribute to the implementation of the Framework by supporting knowledge exchange, technical and scientific cooperation, capacity-building and development, and coordinated action in the implementation of the updated programme of work;"},{"t":"9. Encourages Parties [to apply a human rights-based approach in the implementation of][to implement] the updated programme of work, consistent with section C of the Framework and Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities, including by ensuring the full, equitable, inclusive and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, [recognizing their own governance systems,] [women, girls and youth, and, as appropriate, the protection of environmental human rights defenders];"},{"t":"10. Invites Parties to take into consideration findings from relevant assessments of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services when implementing the updated programme of work and to engage in the preparations of the methodological assessment on integrated biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning and ecological connectivity;"},{"t":"[11. [Decides to establish a fifth programme element][Endorses a cross-cutting complementary activity] on ecological connectivity within the programme of work, as set out in section II of the annex to the present decision, recognizing ecological connectivity as one of several foundational conditions for achieving ecologically representative, well-connected, effectively conserved and managed, and equitably governed systems[ of protected areas and other effective areabased conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], to support the development and implementation of actions to meet the relevant targets of the Framework[, in particular Targets 1 to 6, 9 and 12];]"},{"t":"[12. Invites Parties to reinforce ecological connectivity in the implementation of the updated programme of work, in line with the relevant complementary activities set out in the annex to the present decision and in support of the implementation of the Framework;] [13. Decides to consider at its eighteenth meeting, as appropriate, whether additional guidance related to ecological connectivity is required under the Convention, taking into account the findings of the methodological assessment of integrated biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning and 2/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"4.\n[認可] 本決議附件所載之用於進一步或改進指引的補充活動，作為支持綱要實施工作計畫之更新，並特別關注目標 3；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n[認可] 本決議附件所載之用於進一步或改進指引的補充活動，作為支持綱要實施工作計畫之更新，並特別關注目標 3；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"5.\n**鼓勵**締約方及其他政府，在符合國家情況、立法與優先事項之前提下，將更新後的工作計畫納入開發與實施行動中，以達成綱要之相關目標，特別是目標 3；","html":"<p>5.<br />\n<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方及其他政府，在符合國家情況、立法與優先事項之前提下，將更新後的工作計畫納入開發與實施行動中，以達成綱要之相關目標，特別是目標 3；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[6. **邀請** [已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家義務之締約方] 締約方、其他政府、次國家級與地方政府 [以及非主權出資者，例如財務機制]、私營部門與慈善組織，根據《生物多樣性公約》第 [20] [及 21] 條以及綱要目標 19，從所有來源動員新的、額外的、可預測的、充足且可取得的財務資源，以支持更新後工作計畫之實施，特別是針對開發中國家，包括小島嶼開發中國家，並符合公約第 20 條第 6 項之規定；]","html":"<p>[6. <strong>邀請</strong> [已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家義務之締約方] 締約方、其他政府、次國家級與地方政府 [以及非主權出資者，例如財務機制]、私營部門與慈善組織，根據《生物多樣性公約》第 [20] [及 21] 條以及綱要目標 19，從所有來源動員新的、額外的、可預測的、充足且可取得的財務資源，以支持更新後工作計畫之實施，特別是針對開發中國家，包括小島嶼開發中國家，並符合公約第 20 條第 6 項之規定；]</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[7. **認識到** 動員可預測、充足且永續的實施手段之重要性，包括透過財務資源、技術與科學合作以及能力建構，以確保更新後工作計畫之有效實施；]","html":"<p>[7. <strong>認識到</strong> 動員可預測、充足且永續的實施手段之重要性，包括透過財務資源、技術與科學合作以及能力建構，以確保更新後工作計畫之有效實施；]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"8.\n**邀請** 相關生物多樣性相關公約與其他多邊環境協議之秘書處、國際組織與聯合國實體，包括生態連結全球夥伴關係、原住民族與地方社區，包括私營部門、學術界、非政府組織、女性、青年及其他相關利害關係人，透過支持知識交換、技術與科學合作、能力建構與發展，以及在實施更新後工作計畫中的協調行動，為綱要之實施做出貢獻；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong> 相關生物多樣性相關公約與其他多邊環境協議之秘書處、國際組織與聯合國實體，包括生態連結全球夥伴關係、原住民族與地方社區，包括私營部門、學術界、非政府組織、女性、青年及其他相關利害關係人，透過支持知識交換、技術與科學合作、能力建構與發展，以及在實施更新後工作計畫中的協調行動，為綱要之實施做出貢獻；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"9.\n**鼓勵** 締約方 [在實施更新後工作計畫時採用以人權為基礎的方法][實施] 更新後的工作計畫，且應與綱要 C 節以及公約中與原住民族與地方社區相關之第 8(j) 條及其他條文保持一致，包括確保原住民族與地方社區之充分、公平、包容且有效的參與，[承認其自身的治理體系，] [女性、女孩與青年，並在適當時，保護環境人權捍衛者]；","html":"<p>9.<br />\n<strong>鼓勵</strong> 締約方 [在實施更新後工作計畫時採用以人權為基礎的方法][實施] 更新後的工作計畫，且應與綱要 C 節以及公約中與原住民族與地方社區相關之第 8(j) 條及其他條文保持一致，包括確保原住民族與地方社區之充分、公平、包容且有效的參與，[承認其自身的治理體系，] [女性、女孩與青年，並在適當時，保護環境人權捍衛者]；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"10.\n**邀請** 締約方在實施更新後工作計畫時，考慮來自政府間科學－政策平台關於生物多樣性與生態系服務之相關評估結果，並參與關於整合生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結之方法論評估之準備工作；","html":"<p>10.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong> 締約方在實施更新後工作計畫時，考慮來自政府間科學－政策平台關於生物多樣性與生態系服務之相關評估結果，並參與關於整合生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結之方法論評估之準備工作；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[11. [決定建立工作計畫中之第五個計畫要素][認可一項跨領域補充活動] 關於生態連結，如本決議附件第二節所述，並認識到生態連結是達成具生態代表性、連結良好、受有效保育與管理，且治理公平之系統 [之保護區與保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地] 的數個基礎條件之一，以支持開發與實施行動以達成綱要之相關目標[, 特別是目標 1 至 6、9 與 12]；]","html":"<p>[11. [決定建立工作計畫中之第五個計畫要素][認可一項跨領域補充活動] 關於生態連結，如本決議附件第二節所述，並認識到生態連結是達成具生態代表性、連結良好、受有效保育與管理，且治理公平之系統 [之保護區與保育共生地，並在適用時承認原住民族與傳統領地] 的數個基礎條件之一，以支持開發與實施行動以達成綱要之相關目標[, 特別是目標 1 至 6、9 與 12]；]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"[12. **邀請** 締約方在實施更新後工作計畫時強化生態連結，並與本決議附件所載之相關補充活動一致，以支持綱要之實施；]","html":"<p>[12. <strong>邀請</strong> 締約方在實施更新後工作計畫時強化生態連結，並與本決議附件所載之相關補充活動一致，以支持綱要之實施；]</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[13. **決定** 在其第十八次會議中，視適當時，考慮在公約下是否需要與生態連結相關之額外指引，並將整合生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估結果，以及","html":"<p>[13. <strong>決定</strong> 在其第十八次會議中，視適當時，考慮在公約下是否需要與生態連結相關之額外指引，並將整合生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估結果，以及</p>","en":[8]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p003.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"ecological connectivity of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services and other relevant scientific and technical information, as well as experiences in implementing the Framework and progress in the implementation of the programme of work;]"},{"t":"14. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources and avoiding duplication with other ongoing initiatives and relevant programmes of work:"},{"t":"(a) To further support the Target 3 Community of Practice as a flexible, inclusive and voluntary platform, with a view to facilitating coordination, knowledge exchange and implementation support, and to invite indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth, relevant organizations and initiatives to participate in the Community;"},{"t":"(b) To collaborate with the regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres and other relevant partners in order to deliver targeted scientific and technical support to Parties for meeting Target 3 of the Framework, based on the best available information and the best practices identified pursuant to subparagraph (c) (vii) below;"},{"t":"(c) To compile, with input from Parties, other Governments, [subnational and local governments], relevant organizations and other stakeholders[, within their respective mandates, and recognizing traditional territories, where applicable], a synthesis report on experiences, lessons learned and different approaches, as well as relevant scientific information, including the findings of the assessments of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services that support the achievement of Target 3 of the Framework and the implementation of the programme of work [in a manner consistent with Target 3] [, with particular focus on the following areas:"},{"t":"(i) Equitable governance approaches, including the recognition and respect of the rights and contributions of indigenous peoples and local communities and other groups, including through the implementation of relevant targets of the Framework;"},{"t":"(ii) Ecological integrity, representativeness, effective conservation, ecosystem restoration and resilience, and ecological connectivity across terrestrial, wetland, inland water, coastal and marine ecosystems, including in the context of climate change;"},{"t":"(iii) The recognition of indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable [under Target 3 of the Framework], including by applying differentiated approaches for indigenous peoples in voluntary isolation and initial contact[, in line with the principles of no contact, intangibility and precaution], based on the outcomes of Tasks 1.1 and 1.2 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 2030, as contained in decision 17/xx;"},{"t":"(iv) Gender equality and gender‑responsive and intergenerational approaches, and the integration of traditional knowledge, in planning, governance and [the] management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable];"},{"t":"(v) The integration of [well-connected and equitably governed systems of] [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into broader landscapes and seascapes [and the ocean], across areas within and beyond national jurisdiction,[ in line with [the mandates of the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction, 5 the International Maritime Organization, the International Seabed Authority, regional fisheries management organizations and other] relevant"},{"t":"5 A/CONF.232/2023/4."},{"t":"3/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"非正式文件，關於議程項目 17 (c) – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>非正式文件，關於議程項目 17 (c) – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台之生態連結性及其他相關科學與技術資訊，以及執行綱要之經驗與工作計畫執行進度；]","html":"<p>生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台之生態連結性及其他相關科學與技術資訊，以及執行綱要之經驗與工作計畫執行進度；]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"14. **請求**執行秘書，在資源可用且避免與其他進行中之倡議及相關工作計畫重複之前提下：","html":"<p>14. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書，在資源可用且避免與其他進行中之倡議及相關工作計畫重複之前提下：</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(a) 進一步支持目標 3 實務社群，將其作為一個具彈性、包容且自願性的平台，以促進協調、知識交流與執行支援，並**邀請**原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、相關組織與倡議參與該社群；","html":"<p>(a) 進一步支持目標 3 實務社群，將其作為一個具彈性、包容且自願性的平台，以促進協調、知識交流與執行支援，並<strong>邀請</strong>原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、相關組織與倡議參與該社群；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(b) 與區域及次區域技術與科學合作支援中心及其他相關夥伴合作，基於最佳可用資訊以及根據下文第 (c) (vii) 小項所識別之最佳實務，為締約方提供具針對性的科學與技術支援，以達成綱要之目標 3；","html":"<p>(b) 與區域及次區域技術與科學合作支援中心及其他相關夥伴合作，基於最佳可用資訊以及根據下文第 (c) (vii) 小項所識別之最佳實務，為締約方提供具針對性的科學與技術支援，以達成綱要之目標 3；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(c) 在締約方、其他政府、[次國家級與地方政府]、相關組織及其他利害關係人[在其各自職權範圍內，並在適用時承認傳統領地]之參與下，編製一份關於經驗、經驗教訓與不同方法，以及相關科學資訊之綜合報告，包括生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台評估結果，以支持達成綱要目標 3 及工作計畫之執行[且方式應與目標 3 一致] [, 並特別關注以下領域：","html":"<p>(c) 在締約方、其他政府、[次國家級與地方政府]、相關組織及其他利害關係人[在其各自職權範圍內，並在適用時承認傳統領地]之參與下，編製一份關於經驗、經驗教訓與不同方法，以及相關科學資訊之綜合報告，包括生物多樣性與生態系服務政府間科學－政策平台評估結果，以支持達成綱要目標 3 及工作計畫之執行[且方式應與目標 3 一致] [, 並特別關注以下領域：</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(i) 公平的治理方法，包括承認並尊重原住民族與地方社區及其他群體之權利與貢獻，其方式包括透過執行綱要之相關目標；","html":"<p>(i) 公平的治理方法，包括承認並尊重原住民族與地方社區及其他群體之權利與貢獻，其方式包括透過執行綱要之相關目標；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(ii) 陸域、濕地、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之生態完整性、代表性、有效保育、生態系復育與韌性，以及生態連結性，包括在氣候變遷背景下；","html":"<p>(ii) 陸域、濕地、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之生態完整性、代表性、有效保育、生態系復育與韌性，以及生態連結性，包括在氣候變遷背景下；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(iii) 在適用情況下對原住民及傳統領地之承認[於綱要目標 3 之下]，包括針對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態之原住民族，採用差異化方法[, 並符合不接觸、不可侵犯與預防原則]，其基礎為決議 17/xx 中所載關於 2030 年前針對原住民族與地方社區之第 8(j) 條及公約其他條款工作計畫之任務 1.1 與 1.2 之結果；","html":"<p>(iii) 在適用情況下對原住民及傳統領地之承認[於綱要目標 3 之下]，包括針對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態之原住民族，採用差異化方法[, 並符合不接觸、不可侵犯與預防原則]，其基礎為決議 17/xx 中所載關於 2030 年前針對原住民族與地方社區之第 8(j) 條及公約其他條款工作計畫之任務 1.1 與 1.2 之結果；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(iv) 在規劃、治理及[該]管理[保護區與保育共生地，在適用時承認原住民與傳統領地]中，納入性別平等、具性別回應性與跨世代之方法，以及傳統知識之整合；","html":"<p>(iv) 在規劃、治理及[該]管理[保護區與保育共生地，在適用時承認原住民與傳統領地]中，納入性別平等、具性別回應性與跨世代之方法，以及傳統知識之整合；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(v) 將[具良好連結性且治理公平之][保護區與保育共生地，在適用時承認原住民與傳統領地，]整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景[及海洋]之中，涵蓋國家管轄範圍內與範圍外之區域，[並與[聯合國海洋法公約下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用協定之職權、國際海事組織、國際海底管理局、區域漁業管理組織及其他]相關國際組織，包括透過生物多樣性包容性與參與式空間規劃；","html":"<p>(v) 將[具良好連結性且治理公平之][保護區與保育共生地，在適用時承認原住民與傳統領地，]整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景[及海洋]之中，涵蓋國家管轄範圍內與範圍外之區域，[並與[聯合國海洋法公約下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用協定之職權、國際海事組織、國際海底管理局、區域漁業管理組織及其他]相關國際組織，包括透過生物多樣性包容性與參與式空間規劃；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"---\n5 A/CONF.232/2023/4.","html":"<hr />\n<p>5 A/CONF.232/2023/4.</p>","en":[11,12]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p004.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"international organizations,] including through biodiversity‑inclusive and participatory spatial planning;"},{"t":"(vi) The identification and prioritization of areas of particular importance for biodiversity, ecosystem functions and services, and biocultural diversity, including underrepresented ecosystems and areas supporting ecological networks below ground;"},{"t":"(vii) Planning, governance and [the] effective management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including the integration of climate change considerations and participatory risk assessment into species and ecosystem conservation, as well as the management of human-wildlife conflict to promote coexistence, as key conditions for achieving management effectiveness, including examples and best practices for other effective area-based conservation measures;"},{"t":"(viii) Ecological networks, conservation mosaics, climate‑informed spatial planning and corridor design, ecological connectivity on varying scales, transboundary conservation and its contribution to peace, and restoration, including in urban and peri-urban contexts;"},{"t":"(ix) Monitoring and evaluation systems [for protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including through biodiversity monitoring and the use of relevant new technologies, community-based monitoring, the strengthening of national biodiversity databases, among other relevant dimensions, and, where possible, the principles of findability, accessibility, interoperability and reusability (FAIR) and of collective benefit, authority to control, responsibility and ethics (CARE)[, in accordance with national circumstances and legislation];"},{"t":"(x) Sustainable finance approaches, innovative financial mechanisms, including from public and private sources [and environmental and social safeguards], relevant to the implementation of Target 3 of the Framework according to national priorities and in line with the implementation of their national biodiversity strategies and action plans, including direct and accessible financing approaches for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth;"},{"t":"(xi) Good practices related to access to information, participation in decision-making, access to justice and the protection of environmental human rights defenders, consistent with Target 22 of the Framework;]"},{"t":"(d) To report on progress made in the implementation of the present decision to the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties."},{"t":"Annex"},{"t":"Update to the programme of work on [protected and conserved areas][protected areas and [areas with] other effective area-based conservation measures[, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]]"},{"t":"1. The table below shows the mapping of the targets of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework6 against complementary activities that could support the implementation of the programme of work.7 It highlights areas of strong alignment, opportunities to strengthen existing provisions and gaps where further development is needed. It is based on the findings of a strategic review of the programme, related submissions and a peer review analysis. The activities are"},{"t":"6 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"7 Decision VII/28, annex."},{"t":"4/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(vi)\n對生物多樣性、生態系功能與服務，以及生物文化多樣性具有特別重要性之區域進行識別與優先排序，包括代表性不足之生態系，以及支持地下生態網絡之區域；","html":"<p>(vi)<br />\n對生物多樣性、生態系功能與服務，以及生物文化多樣性具有特別重要性之區域進行識別與優先排序，包括代表性不足之生態系，以及支持地下生態網絡之區域；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(vii)\n規劃、治理與[對]有效管理[保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括將氣候變遷考量與參與式風險評估納入物種與生態系保育，以及管理人與野生動物衝突以促進共存，作為達成管理成效之關鍵條件，包括保育共生地之範例與最佳實務；","html":"<p>(vii)<br />\n規劃、治理與[對]有效管理[保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括將氣候變遷考量與參與式風險評估納入物種與生態系保育，以及管理人與野生動物衝突以促進共存，作為達成管理成效之關鍵條件，包括保育共生地之範例與最佳實務；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(viii)\n生態網絡、保育鑲嵌、具氣候資訊之空間規劃與廊道設計、不同尺度之生態連結性、跨境保育及其對和平之貢獻，以及復育，包括在城市與近郊環境中之復育；","html":"<p>(viii)<br />\n生態網絡、保育鑲嵌、具氣候資訊之空間規劃與廊道設計、不同尺度之生態連結性、跨境保育及其對和平之貢獻，以及復育，包括在城市與近郊環境中之復育；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(ix)\n監測與評估系統[保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過生物多樣性監測與相關新技術之使用、以社區為基礎之監測、強化國家生物多樣性資料庫等其他相關面向，且在可能情況下，遵循可發現性、可取得性、互通性與可重用性 (FAIR) 以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理 (CARE) 之原則[，並符合國家情況與立法]；","html":"<p>(ix)<br />\n監測與評估系統[保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過生物多樣性監測與相關新技術之使用、以社區為基礎之監測、強化國家生物多樣性資料庫等其他相關面向，且在可能情況下，遵循可發現性、可取得性、互通性與可重用性 (FAIR) 以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理 (CARE) 之原則[，並符合國家情況與立法]；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(x)\n與實施綱要目標 3 相關之永續金融方法、創新財務機制，包括來自公共與私人來源[以及環境與社會安全保障]，應根據國家優先事項並符合其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之實施，包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之直接且易於取得之融資方法；","html":"<p>(x)<br />\n與實施綱要目標 3 相關之永續金融方法、創新財務機制，包括來自公共與私人來源[以及環境與社會安全保障]，應根據國家優先事項並符合其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之實施，包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之直接且易於取得之融資方法；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(xi)\n與綱要目標 22 一致，關於資訊取得、參與決策、訴諸司法以及保護環境人權捍衛者之良好實務；]","html":"<p>(xi)<br />\n與綱要目標 22 一致，關於資訊取得、參與決策、訴諸司法以及保護環境人權捍衛者之良好實務；]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(d) 向科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構報告本決議實施進展，該會議應於第十八次締約方大會召開前舉行。","html":"<p>(d) 向科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構報告本決議實施進展，該會議應於第十八次締約方大會召開前舉行。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"附件\n關於[保護與保育區域][保護區與[具有]保育共生地之區域[, 在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地]]之工作計畫更新","html":"<p>附件<br />\n關於[保護與保育區域][保護區與[具有]保育共生地之區域[, 在適用情況下，應承認原住民族與傳統領地]]之工作計畫更新</p>","en":[9,10]},{"md":"1.\n下表顯示了將昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要$^6$之目標，與可能支持工作計畫實施之補充活動進行對照之情況$^7$。其強調了高度一致之領域、強化現有規定之機會，以及需要進一步發展之缺口。此內容係基於對工作計畫之策略性審查、相關提交文件及同儕審查分析之結果。相關活動為","html":"<p>1.<br />\n下表顯示了將昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>6</sup>之目標，與可能支持工作計畫實施之補充活動進行對照之情況<sup>7</sup>。其強調了高度一致之領域、強化現有規定之機會，以及需要進一步發展之缺口。此內容係基於對工作計畫之策略性審查、相關提交文件及同儕審查分析之結果。相關活動為</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"---\n$^6$ 決議 15/4，附件。\n$^7$ 決議 VII/28，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>6</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>7</sup> 決議 VII/28，附件。</p>","en":[12,13,14]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p005.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"categorized as follows: (A) activities that have existing strong alignment with Target 3 of the Framework and its interlinkages with other targets; (B) activities that address targets that are partially covered by the programme of work and where implementation can be strengthened; and (C) activities for further developing areas that the programme of work does not cover or only covers in a limited manner and where additional guidance is needed. For Targets 9, 13, 16, 17 and 18, no specific actions [relevant to protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] are proposed."},{"t":"2. The implementation of the updated programme of work should be conducted in line with section C of the Framework, [in particular by following a human rights-based approach,] and in accordance with national circumstances, legislation and priorities."},{"t":"I. Complementary activities to strengthen the programme of work on [protected and conserved areas][protected areas and [areas with] other effective area-based conservation measures[, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]] and its alignment with the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"Targets of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"Complementary activities"},{"t":"Category"},{"t":"Target 1"},{"t":"1. Integrate [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into broader landscape and seascape planning to improve, in accordance with national legislation, biodiversity outcomes, ecological representativeness and connectivity, through participatory and biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning processes, while recognizing and respecting the rights of indigenous peoples and local communities."},{"t":"[1 bis Additional complementary activities on ecological connectivity.]"},{"t":"A"},{"t":"Target 2"},{"t":"2. Promote the restoration of degraded ecosystems [within protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], and beyond, including buffer zones, ecological corridors, [soil biodiversity, in particular fungal biodiversity,8] and inland water ecosystems, with a view to restoring ecological integrity and ecological connectivity across landscapes and seascapes, including through the development of criteria for identifying priority restoration areas and approaches for measuring restoration success, ensuring inclusive and gender-responsive implementation of the restoration efforts[, as appropriate]."},{"t":"[2 bis. Additional complementary activities on ecological connectivity.]"},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 3"},{"t":"3. Incorporate the language, scope and timelines of Target 3 of the Framework across implementation of the programme of work, updating relevant timelines and terminology, and ensuring coherence with related processes carried out under the Convention on Biological Diversity, including the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 2030.9"},{"t":"A"},{"t":"8 As described in Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations and others, State of Knowledge of Soil Biodiversity:"},{"t":"Status, Challenges and Potentialities, Report 2020 (Rome, 2020)."},{"t":"9 Decision 16/4, annex."},{"t":"5/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"分類如下：(A) 與《綱要》目標 3 具有既有強烈一致性及其與其他目標之關聯性的活動；(B) 針對工作計畫部分涵蓋之目標，且其執行可望加強之活動；以及 (C) 針對工作計畫未涵蓋或僅有限度涵蓋，且需要額外指引之領域進行進一步開發之活動。針對目標 9、13、16、17 及 18，未提出任何特定行動 [與保護區及保育共生地相關，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，]。","html":"<p>分類如下：(A) 與《綱要》目標 3 具有既有強烈一致性及其與其他目標之關聯性的活動；(B) 針對工作計畫部分涵蓋之目標，且其執行可望加強之活動；以及 (C) 針對工作計畫未涵蓋或僅有限度涵蓋，且需要額外指引之領域進行進一步開發之活動。針對目標 9、13、16、17 及 18，未提出任何特定行動 [與保護區及保育共生地相關，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，]。</p>","en":[1,2,3,4]},{"md":"2.\n更新後工作計畫之執行，應符合《綱要》C 節之規定，[特別是透過遵循以人權為基礎的方法，] 並根據國家情況、立法與優先事項進行。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n更新後工作計畫之執行，應符合《綱要》C 節之規定，[特別是透過遵循以人權為基礎的方法，] 並根據國家情況、立法與優先事項進行。</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"I.\n旨在強化關於 [保護與保育區域][保護區與 [包含] 保育共生地[, 在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]] 之工作計畫，及其與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》一致性之補充活動","html":"<p>I.<br />\n旨在強化關於 [保護與保育區域][保護區與 [包含] 保育共生地[, 在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]] 之工作計畫，及其與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》一致性之補充活動</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"| 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 目標 1 | 1. 根據國家立法，透過參與式且具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃程序，將 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至更廣泛的陸域與海域規劃中，以改善生物多樣性成果、生態代表性與連結性，同時認可並尊重原住民族與地方社區之權利。 [1 bis 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。] | A |\n| 目標 2 | 2. 促進退化生態系之復育，[於保護區與保育共生地內，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，及其範圍之外，包括緩衝區、生態廊道、[土壤生物多樣性，特別是真菌生物多樣性，8] 以及內陸水域生態系，旨在恢復跨陸域與海域之生態完整性與生態連結性，包括透過制定識別優先復育區域之標準以及衡量復育成功之方法，並確保復育工作之執行具包容性且對性別敏感[，視情況而定]。 [2 bis. 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。] | B |\n| 目標 3 | 3. 在工作計畫之執行過程中，納入《綱要》目標 3 之用語、範圍與時程，更新相關時程與術語，並確保與《生物多樣性公約》下進行之相關程序保持一致，包括關於第 8(j) 條及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關規定之工作計畫至 2030 年。9 | A |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">1. 根據國家立法，透過參與式且具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃程序，將 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至更廣泛的陸域與海域規劃中，以改善生物多樣性成果、生態代表性與連結性，同時認可並尊重原住民族與地方社區之權利。 [1 bis 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">2. 促進退化生態系之復育，[於保護區與保育共生地內，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，及其範圍之外，包括緩衝區、生態廊道、[土壤生物多樣性，特別是真菌生物多樣性，8] 以及內陸水域生態系，旨在恢復跨陸域與海域之生態完整性與生態連結性，包括透過制定識別優先復育區域之標準以及衡量復育成功之方法，並確保復育工作之執行具包容性且對性別敏感[，視情況而定]。 [2 bis. 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 3</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">3. 在工作計畫之執行過程中，納入《綱要》目標 3 之用語、範圍與時程，更新相關時程與術語，並確保與《生物多樣性公約》下進行之相關程序保持一致，包括關於第 8(j) 條及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關規定之工作計畫至 2030 年。9</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[15,16,17,18,19]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[20]},{"md":"$^8$ 如聯合國糧食及農業組織（FAO）等所載，《土壤生物多樣性現況：地位、挑戰與潛力，2020 年報告》（羅馬，2020）。\n$^9$ 決議 16/4，附件。","html":"<p><sup>8</sup> 如聯合國糧食及農業組織（FAO）等所載，《土壤生物多樣性現況：地位、挑戰與潛力，2020 年報告》（羅馬，2020）。<br />\n<sup>9</sup> 決議 16/4，附件。</p>","en":[21,22,23,24]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p006.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"Targets of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"Complementary activities"},{"t":"Category"},{"t":"4. Strengthen guidance related to improving monitoring, reporting and evaluation systems for terrestrial, inland waters, coastal and marine ecosystems to improve the assessment of biodiversity outcomes, including in relation to ecological representativeness, connectivity, integrity, conservation effectiveness, management effectiveness, governance quality, species population trends and through the use of appropriately indicators of the monitoring framework for the KunmingMontreal Global Biodiversity Framework,10 as well as disaggregated indicators, including, as appropriate, by ecosystem type and level of protection."},{"t":"5. Enhance guidance related to the recognition, respect, promotion and protection of indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable, in the context of Target 3 of the Framework, in a manner consistent with the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities. This encompasses differentiated approaches to ensure comprehensive protection, including for indigenous peoples in voluntary isolation and initial contact, in line with the principles of no contact, intangibility and precaution, in accordance with national circumstances."},{"t":"6. Increase the uptake of practical frameworks, guidance, emerging innovative tools, case studies and national experiences, lessons learned and different approaches to support the implementation of Target 3 of the Framework, including the definition and prioritization of areas of particular importance for biodiversity, ecological networks, corridor design for climate adaptation, large‑scale ecological connectivity, including ecological processes below ground, other effective areabased conservation measures and transboundary conservation."},{"t":"7. Strengthen the operationalization of equitable and effective governance in [the] planning and management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] [and a human rights-based approach] consistent with section C of the Framework, including by, as appropriate, shifting from beneficiary‑based approaches to recognizing, respecting, promoting and protecting the rights and contributions of indigenous peoples and local communities; promoting standards and good practices for participation, shared governance and co‑management arrangements; ensuring culturally appropriate access to information; respecting and strengthening, where applicable, the implementation of free, prior and informed consent,11 [consistent with national circumstances and legislation and international instruments]."},{"t":"8. Strengthen inclusive monitoring, reporting and evaluation systems [for protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including by identifying available tools, and facilitate the use of relevant new technologies to better assess ecological representativeness, integrity and connectivity, biodiversity outcomes, management effectiveness, governance quality, species"},{"t":"10 Decision 15/5, annex I, as updated in decision 16/31, and decision 17/-- on planning, monitoring, reporting and review."},{"t":"11 “Free, prior and informed consent” refers to the tripartite terminology of “prior and informed consent”, “free, prior and"},{"t":"informed consent” and “approval and involvement”."},{"t":"6/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n|  | 4. 強化與改善陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系監測、報告與評估系統相關之指引，以改善生物多樣性成果之評估，包括與生態代表性、連結性、完整性、保育成效、管理成效、治理品質、物種族群趨勢相關之評估，並透過使用昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之適當指標，10 以及分項指標，包括視情況依生態系類型與保護等級進行分類。 5. 在綱要目標 3 之脈絡下，強化與承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）相關之指引，其方式應與關於第 8(j) 條之工作計畫，以及公約中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他條文保持一致。這包括採取差異化方法以確保全面性的保護，包括針對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態之原住民族，並應符合不接觸、不可侵犯及預防原則，並視國家情況而定。 6. 增加實務框架、指引、新興創新工具、個案研究、國家經驗、經驗教訓及不同方法之運用，以支持綱要目標 3 之實施，包括對生物多樣性特別重要區域之定義與優先順序劃定、生態網路、因應氣候調適之廊道設計、大規模生態連結性（包括地下生態過程）、保育共生地以及跨境保育。 7. 強化在[該]規劃與管理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] [以及基於人權之方法] 中，公平且有效治理之具體化，且應與綱要 C 節保持一致，包括視情況透過從以受益者為基礎之方法，轉向承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與地方社區之權利與貢獻；促進參與、共同治理與共同管理安排之標準與良好實務；確保文化適切之資訊取得；並在適用情況下，尊重並強化自由、事先及知情同意之實施，11 [並與國家情況、國內立法及國際文書保持一致]。 8. 強化具包容性之監測、報告與評估系統 [針對保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過識別可用工具，並促進相關新技術之使用，以更佳地評估生態代表性、完整性與連結性、生物多樣性成果、管理成效、治理品質、物種 |  |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">4. 強化與改善陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系監測、報告與評估系統相關之指引，以改善生物多樣性成果之評估，包括與生態代表性、連結性、完整性、保育成效、管理成效、治理品質、物種族群趨勢相關之評估，並透過使用昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之適當指標，10 以及分項指標，包括視情況依生態系類型與保護等級進行分類。 5. 在綱要目標 3 之脈絡下，強化與承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與傳統領地（如適用）相關之指引，其方式應與關於第 8(j) 條之工作計畫，以及公約中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他條文保持一致。這包括採取差異化方法以確保全面性的保護，包括針對處於自願隔離與初步接觸狀態之原住民族，並應符合不接觸、不可侵犯及預防原則，並視國家情況而定。 6. 增加實務框架、指引、新興創新工具、個案研究、國家經驗、經驗教訓及不同方法之運用，以支持綱要目標 3 之實施，包括對生物多樣性特別重要區域之定義與優先順序劃定、生態網路、因應氣候調適之廊道設計、大規模生態連結性（包括地下生態過程）、保育共生地以及跨境保育。 7. 強化在[該]規劃與管理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] [以及基於人權之方法] 中，公平且有效治理之具體化，且應與綱要 C 節保持一致，包括視情況透過從以受益者為基礎之方法，轉向承認、尊重、促進及保護原住民族與地方社區之權利與貢獻；促進參與、共同治理與共同管理安排之標準與良好實務；確保文化適切之資訊取得；並在適用情況下，尊重並強化自由、事先及知情同意之實施，11 [並與國家情況、國內立法及國際文書保持一致]。 8. 強化具包容性之監測、報告與評估系統 [針對保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過識別可用工具，並促進相關新技術之使用，以更佳地評估生態代表性、完整性與連結性、生物多樣性成果、管理成效、治理品質、物種</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"---\n$^{10}$ 決議 15/5 附件 I，經決議 16/31 更新，以及關於規劃、監測、報告與審查之決議 17/--。\n$^{11}$ 「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>10</sup> 決議 15/5 附件 I，經決議 16/31 更新，以及關於規劃、監測、報告與審查之決議 17/--。<br />\n<sup>11</sup> 「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。</p>","en":[11,12,13,14]},{"md":"6/11","html":"<p>6/11</p>","en":[15]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p007.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"Targets of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"Complementary activities"},{"t":"Category"},{"t":"population trends, relevant indicators of the monitoring framework, as well as [gender-]disaggregated indicators."},{"t":"9. Promote the use of relevant and new approaches for ecological integrity and connectivity in the planning and management [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including through the development of ecological networks, ecological corridors, stepping stones and transboundary connectivity initiatives and corridor design for climate adaptation across wider landscapes and seascapes."},{"t":"10. Strengthen the integration of climate change considerations into the planning and management of [protected and other effective areabased conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including ecological corridors. [10 bis. Additional complementary activities on ecological connectivity.]"},{"t":"Target 4"},{"t":"11. Strengthen capacities for planning and management through participatory risk assessment, rapid response mechanisms, where possible, and inclusive community engagements and the integration of traditional knowledge in addressing human-wildlife conflict and promoting coexistence[ in protected areas and other effective areabased conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]."},{"t":"12. Integrate effective management of human-wildlife interactions, including human-wildlife conflict risk assessment, in order to minimize conflict to promote coexistence [in the context of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]. [12 bis Additional complementary activities on ecological connectivity.]"},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 5"},{"t":"13. Address and manage the use of wild species [within protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] where such use is allowed, in a manner that mitigates risks to native biodiversity and human health, consistent with site‑specific conservation objectives and zoning, while preventing overexploitation and ensuring sustainable, legal and safe use at all stages, including through participatory biodiversity monitoring and the application of One Health risk assessment frameworks, as appropriate, and respecting and protecting the customary sustainable use practices of indigenous peoples and local communities."},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 6"},{"t":"14. Strengthen the prediction, prevention, early detection, control or eradication of and the rapid response to invasive alien species[ in protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including through community-based monitoring, surveillance systems, and biosecurity and trade-related measures.12"},{"t":"15. Strengthen guidelines, where applicable, for the development and implementation of national and regional plans for the management of"},{"t":"B"},{"t":"12 Any international measures should be implemented in compliance with the Agreement on the Application of Sanitary and"},{"t":"Phytosanitary Measures of the World Trade Organization and with the International Plant Protection Convention."},{"t":"7/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n|  | 族群趨勢、監測架構之相關指標，以及 [性別] 分層指標。 9. 促進在規劃與管理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 時，使用與生態完整性及連結性相關之新方法，包括透過開發生態網路、生態廊道、踏腳石以及跨國界連結倡議，以及針對更廣泛的陸域與海域景觀進行氣候調適之廊道設計。 10. 加強將氣候變遷考量整合至 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 之規劃與管理中，包括生態廊道。 [10 bis. 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。] |  |\n| 目標 4 | 11. 透過參與式風險評估、在可能情況下建立快速反應機制、包容性社區參與，以及在處理人與野生動物衝突與促進共存時整合傳統知識，以強化規劃與管理之能力[於保護區與保育共生地中，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 12. 整合人與野生動物互動之有效管理，包括人與野生動物衝突風險評估，以將衝突降至最低並促進共存 [於保護區與保育共生地之脈絡下，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 [12 bis 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。] | B |\n| 目標 5 | 13. 針對並管理野生物種之利用 [於保護區與保育共生地內，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，]，在允許此類利用之情況下，應以減輕對原生生物多樣性與人類健康風險之方式進行，並與特定場域之保育目標及分區規劃保持一致，同時防止過度開發，並確保在所有階段皆為永續、合法且安全之利用，包括透過參與式生物多樣性監測以及適當應用健康一體風險評估架構，並尊重且保護原住民族與地方社區之慣習性永續利用實務。 | B |\n| 目標 6 | 14. 強化對外來入侵種之預測、預防、早期偵測、控制或根除，以及快速反應之能力[於保護區與保育共生地中，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過以社區為基礎之監測、監測系統，以及生物安全與貿易相關措施。12 15. 在適用情況下，強化開發與執行國家及區域計畫之指南，以進行管理 | B |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">族群趨勢、監測架構之相關指標，以及 [性別] 分層指標。 9. 促進在規劃與管理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 時，使用與生態完整性及連結性相關之新方法，包括透過開發生態網路、生態廊道、踏腳石以及跨國界連結倡議，以及針對更廣泛的陸域與海域景觀進行氣候調適之廊道設計。 10. 加強將氣候變遷考量整合至 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 之規劃與管理中，包括生態廊道。 [10 bis. 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">11. 透過參與式風險評估、在可能情況下建立快速反應機制、包容性社區參與，以及在處理人與野生動物衝突與促進共存時整合傳統知識，以強化規劃與管理之能力[於保護區與保育共生地中，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 12. 整合人與野生動物互動之有效管理，包括人與野生動物衝突風險評估，以將衝突降至最低並促進共存 [於保護區與保育共生地之脈絡下，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 [12 bis 關於生態連結性的額外補充活動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 5</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">13. 針對並管理野生物種之利用 [於保護區與保育共生地內，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，]，在允許此類利用之情況下，應以減輕對原生生物多樣性與人類健康風險之方式進行，並與特定場域之保育目標及分區規劃保持一致，同時防止過度開發，並確保在所有階段皆為永續、合法且安全之利用，包括透過參與式生物多樣性監測以及適當應用健康一體風險評估架構，並尊重且保護原住民族與地方社區之慣習性永續利用實務。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 6</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">14. 強化對外來入侵種之預測、預防、早期偵測、控制或根除，以及快速反應之能力[於保護區與保育共生地中，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，包括透過以社區為基礎之監測、監測系統，以及生物安全與貿易相關措施。12 15. 在適用情況下，強化開發與執行國家及區域計畫之指南，以進行管理</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"---\n$^{12}$ 任何國際措施之實施，均應符合世界貿易組織《衛生與植物衛生措施協定》及《國際植物保護公約》。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>12</sup> 任何國際措施之實施，均應符合世界貿易組織《衛生與植物衛生措施協定》及《國際植物保護公約》。</p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p008.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"Targets of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"Complementary activities"},{"t":"Category"},{"t":"invasive alien species and pathways of introduction into protected areas."},{"t":"8/11"},{"t":"Target 7"},{"t":"16. Address pollution pressures[, including plastic pollution, pollution from hazardous substances, pesticide use and run-off, and noise and light pollution,] from all sources [affecting protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], cumulative impacts and land-sea"},{"t":"interactions."},{"t":"Target 8"},{"t":"17. Strengthen the integration of climate change considerations into the planning and management of [protected and other effective areabased conservation measures and indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including ecological corridors, by scaling up related response measures that promote resilience in order to minimize the negative impacts of climate change, while ensuring ecological integrity."},{"t":"18. Promote system design for climate adaptation and resilience that anticipates future range shifts, including by identifying additional climate refugia, connectivity corridors[, soil biodiversity, in particular fungal biodiversity,] and areas of future biodiversity importance."},{"t":"C"},{"t":"Target 9"},{"t":"[19. No specific actions identified.]"},{"t":"[n/a]"},{"t":"Target 10"},{"t":"20. Strengthen guidance on the sustainable management of productive landscapes and biodiversity-friendly practices to support[, while being distinguished from,] [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] and improvements in biodiversity, ecological connectivity, ecosystem functions and resilience across landscapes and seascapes, in particular by promoting nature-based solutions and/or ecosystem-based approaches and integrated land-use planning approaches, recognizing the value of traditional knowledge and practices [and ways to distinguish such activities from those that fall under Target 3 of the Framework]."},{"t":"C"},{"t":"Target 11"},{"t":"21. Highlight the role of [protected areas and other effective areabased conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] in restoring, maintaining and enhancing nature’s contributions to people, including ecosystem functions and services, [including water security, coastal protection, pollinators and food security,] as well as strengthen capacities to measure and value those functions and services."},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 12"},{"t":"22. Integrate [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into urban and peri-urban planning, including through green and blue infrastructure, to enhance ecological connectivity, restoration, the conservation of native species and climate change adaptation, and to support physical and mental health and wellbeing, and equitable access to nature especially for the most vulnerable."},{"t":"[22 bis. Additional complementary activities on ecological connectivity.]"},{"t":"C"},{"t":"Target 13"},{"t":"[23. No specific actions identified.]"},{"t":"[n/a]"},{"t":"B"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n|  | 外來入侵種及其進入保護區之路徑。 |  |\n| 目標 7 | 16. 應對來自所有來源之污染壓力[，包括塑膠污染、有害物質污染、農藥使用與逕流，以及噪音與光污染，][影響保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，累積影響及陸海互動。 | B |\n| 目標 8 | 17. 透過擴大相關應對措施以促進韌性，藉此極小化氣候變遷之負面影響，同時確保生態完整性，強化將氣候變遷考量納入 [保護區與保育共生地及原住民族與傳統領地，在適用情況下] 之規劃與管理，包括生態廊道。 18. 推動氣候調適與韌性之系統設計，以預判未來之分布範圍偏移，包括透過識別額外的氣候避難所、連通廊道[、土壤生物多樣性，特別是真菌生物多樣性，] 以及未來具生物多樣性重要性之區域。 | C |\n| 目標 9 | [19. 未識別出特定行動。] | [不適用] |\n| 目標 10 | 20. 強化關於生產性景觀之永續管理與生物多樣性友善做法之指引，以支持[，並與之區隔，] [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 以及景觀與海域之生物多樣性、生態連結性、生態系功能與韌性之改善，特別是透過推動以自然為本的解決方案及／或以生態系為本的方法，以及整合性土地利用規劃方法，並認可傳統知識與做法之價值 [以及區分此類活動與屬於綱要目標 3 之活動之方式]。 | C |\n| 目標 11 | 21. 強調 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 在復育、維持與增強自然對人類之貢獻（包括生態系功能與服務，[包括水安全、海岸防護、傳粉者與糧食安全，]）方面之角色，並強化衡量與評估該等功能與服務之能力。 | B |\n| 目標 12 | 22. 將 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至都市與近郊規劃中，包括透過綠色與藍色基礎設施，以增強生態連結性、復育、原生種保育與氣候變遷調適，並支持身心健康與福祉，以及自然之公平取得，特別是針對最脆弱族群。 [22 bis. 關於生態連結性之額外補充活動。] | C |\n| 目標 13 | [23. 未識別出特定行動。] | [不適用] |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">外來入侵種及其進入保護區之路徑。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 7</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">16. 應對來自所有來源之污染壓力[，包括塑膠污染、有害物質污染、農藥使用與逕流，以及噪音與光污染，][影響保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，累積影響及陸海互動。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 8</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">17. 透過擴大相關應對措施以促進韌性，藉此極小化氣候變遷之負面影響，同時確保生態完整性，強化將氣候變遷考量納入 [保護區與保育共生地及原住民族與傳統領地，在適用情況下] 之規劃與管理，包括生態廊道。 18. 推動氣候調適與韌性之系統設計，以預判未來之分布範圍偏移，包括透過識別額外的氣候避難所、連通廊道[、土壤生物多樣性，特別是真菌生物多樣性，] 以及未來具生物多樣性重要性之區域。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">C</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 9</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[19. 未識別出特定行動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[不適用]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 10</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">20. 強化關於生產性景觀之永續管理與生物多樣性友善做法之指引，以支持[，並與之區隔，] [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 以及景觀與海域之生物多樣性、生態連結性、生態系功能與韌性之改善，特別是透過推動以自然為本的解決方案及／或以生態系為本的方法，以及整合性土地利用規劃方法，並認可傳統知識與做法之價值 [以及區分此類活動與屬於綱要目標 3 之活動之方式]。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">C</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 11</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">21. 強調 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 在復育、維持與增強自然對人類之貢獻（包括生態系功能與服務，[包括水安全、海岸防護、傳粉者與糧食安全，]）方面之角色，並強化衡量與評估該等功能與服務之能力。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 12</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">22. 將 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至都市與近郊規劃中，包括透過綠色與藍色基礎設施，以增強生態連結性、復育、原生種保育與氣候變遷調適，並支持身心健康與福祉，以及自然之公平取得，特別是針對最脆弱族群。 [22 bis. 關於生態連結性之額外補充活動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">C</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 13</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[23. 未識別出特定行動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[不適用]</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p009.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"Targets of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"Complementary activities"},{"t":"Category"},{"t":"Target 14"},{"t":"24. Integrate [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into cross‑sectoral policies, legislation, planning and development processes, where relevant for their planning and effective management."},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 15"},{"t":"25. Support and promote the implementation of legal, administrative or policy measures that encourage and enable businesses and financial institutions to assess, disclose and progressively reduce biodiversity‑related risks, dependencies and impacts [on protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] including across their operations, supply and value chains and portfolios, in order to promote sustainable value chains and reduce risks to biodiversity."},{"t":"26. Facilitate clearer direction on engaging financial actors and the private sector [in support of protected areas and other effective areabased conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] on a voluntary basis to develop the field of conservation, protection and restoration as a key economic area."},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 16"},{"t":"[27. No specific actions identified.]"},{"t":"[27 Alt. Promote synergies between the policies and actions taken to protect and conserve biodiversity, and policies and actions that enable sustainable consumption choices, including through coherent policy frameworks, education, access to reliable information and sector specific approaches, such as sustainable tourism management, contributing to the reduction of consumption footprints and waste generation.]"},{"t":"[n/a]"},{"t":"Target 17"},{"t":"[28. No specific actions identified.]"},{"t":"[n/a]"},{"t":"Target 18"},{"t":"[29. No specific actions identified.]"},{"t":"[n/a]"},{"t":"Target 19"},{"t":"30. Promote the identification of timely, predictable and accessible financial resources from all sources, including domestic, international, public and private resources, for the effective implementation and long-term financial sustainability and institutional resilience [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] [including] in accordance with Article 20 of the Convention, and innovative mechanisms, such as public-private partnerships, especially to support developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States among them, consistent with national priorities and with environmental and social safeguards."},{"t":"31. Promote [direct and] accessible financing for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, where applicable under Target 3 of the Framework, in accordance with national circumstances."},{"t":"A"},{"t":"Target 20"},{"t":"32. Strengthen capacity-building and development, technical and scientific cooperation and technology transfer, on mutually agreed terms, for establishing and managing [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable], including with respect to new technologies and institutional support for the conservation workforce, such as rangers and other relevant personnel."},{"t":"A"},{"t":"9/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 目標 14 | 24. 將 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至跨部門政策、立法、規劃與發展程序中，且在與其規劃及有效管理相關之處。 | B |\n| 目標 15 | 25. 支持並促進法律、行政或政策措施之落實，以鼓勵並使企業與金融機構能夠評估、揭露並逐步減少與生物多樣性相關之風險、依賴性及影響 [對保護區與保育共生地之影響，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 包括其營運、供應鏈、價值鏈及投資組合，以促進永續價值鏈並降低生物多樣性風險。 26. 促進更明確的方向，以自願方式引導金融行為者與私部門 [支持保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 將保育、保護與復育領域發展為關鍵經濟領域。 | B |\n| 目標 16 | [27. 未識別出特定行動。] [27 替代方案。促進保護與保育生物多樣性之政策與行動，以及促進永續消費選擇之政策與行動之間的綜效，包括透過一致的政策框架、教育、取得可靠資訊以及特定產業方法（例如永續旅遊管理），以有助於減少消費足跡與廢棄物產生。] | [不適用] |\n| 目標 17 | [28. 未識別出特定行動。] | [不適用] |\n| 目標 18 | [29. 未識別出特定行動。] | [不適用] |\n| 目標 19 | 30. 促進識別來自所有來源（包括國內、國際、公共與私人資源）之及時、可預測且可取得的財務資源，以確保有效落實並達成長期財務永續性與制度韌性 [針對保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] [包括] 依據公約第二十條，以及創新機制（例如公私夥伴關係），特別是為了支持開發中締約方，尤其是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，且須符合國家優先事項以及環境與社會安全保障。 31. 促進 [直接且] 可取得之資金，用於綱要目標 3 下適用情況下之原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，並符合國家情況。 | A |\n| 目標 20 | 32. 在共同商定條件下，加強能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作以及技術轉移，以建立與管理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，包括針對新技術以及對保育人力（如巡守員及其他相關人員）之制度支持。 | A |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 14</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">24. 將 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 整合至跨部門政策、立法、規劃與發展程序中，且在與其規劃及有效管理相關之處。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 15</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">25. 支持並促進法律、行政或政策措施之落實，以鼓勵並使企業與金融機構能夠評估、揭露並逐步減少與生物多樣性相關之風險、依賴性及影響 [對保護區與保育共生地之影響，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 包括其營運、供應鏈、價值鏈及投資組合，以促進永續價值鏈並降低生物多樣性風險。 26. 促進更明確的方向，以自願方式引導金融行為者與私部門 [支持保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 將保育、保護與復育領域發展為關鍵經濟領域。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 16</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[27. 未識別出特定行動。] [27 替代方案。促進保護與保育生物多樣性之政策與行動，以及促進永續消費選擇之政策與行動之間的綜效，包括透過一致的政策框架、教育、取得可靠資訊以及特定產業方法（例如永續旅遊管理），以有助於減少消費足跡與廢棄物產生。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[不適用]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 17</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[28. 未識別出特定行動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[不適用]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 18</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[29. 未識別出特定行動。]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">[不適用]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 19</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">30. 促進識別來自所有來源（包括國內、國際、公共與私人資源）之及時、可預測且可取得的財務資源，以確保有效落實並達成長期財務永續性與制度韌性 [針對保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] [包括] 依據公約第二十條，以及創新機制（例如公私夥伴關係），特別是為了支持開發中締約方，尤其是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，且須符合國家優先事項以及環境與社會安全保障。 31. 促進 [直接且] 可取得之資金，用於綱要目標 3 下適用情況下之原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，並符合國家情況。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 20</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">32. 在共同商定條件下，加強能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作以及技術轉移，以建立與管理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]，包括針對新技術以及對保育人力（如巡守員及其他相關人員）之制度支持。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[25,26,27,28,29]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p010.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"Targets of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity"},{"t":"Framework"},{"t":"Complementary activities"},{"t":"Category"},{"t":"Target 21"},{"t":"33. Strengthen the application of advances in biodiversity monitoring, data management and knowledge‑sharing through targeted capacity‑building and development on comprehensive biodiversity monitoring and the use of innovative technologies, including digital technologies, remote sensing and national biodiversity databases, to improve monitoring, evaluation, reporting and decision‑making [regarding biodiversity outcomes and ecological connectivity and representativeness, and] relating to [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] including through nationally appropriate approaches and indicators, while strengthening capacities and infrastructure for managing and integrating biodiversity data."},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 22"},{"t":"34. Strengthen access to information and the full, equitable, inclusive, effective and gender-responsive representation and participation of indigenous peoples and local communities in decisionmaking [related to protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]."},{"t":"35. [Ensure] access to justice by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, children, youth and persons with disabilities[, including through the establishment of effective and accessible grievance mechanisms,] in accordance with national legislation and other relevant international agreements, to address issues related to the establishment, management and governance of [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]."},{"t":"36. [Ensure] the full protection of environmental human rights defenders engaged in activities related to [protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable]."},{"t":"B"},{"t":"Target 23"},{"t":"37. Promote gender equality and integrate a gender-responsive approach, including the use of [indicators disaggregated by sex][gender-disaggregated indicators], across the programme of work[, taking gender-based violence into due consideration]."},{"t":"A"},{"t":"[II."},{"t":"Programme element 5: ecological connectivity"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"3. To maintain, enhance and restore structural and functional ecological connectivity across terrestrial, inland water, coastal and marine ecosystems, including by integrating ecologically representative and well-connected systems [of protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, recognizing indigenous and traditional territories, where applicable,] into wider landscapes and seascapes."},{"t":"Goal 5.1 – Integrated planning and implementation"},{"t":"4. Integrate ecological networks, ecological corridors, stepping stones and other measures that maintain, enhance or restore ecological connectivity into biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning, ecosystem restoration, climate change adaptation and relevant sectoral and infrastructure planning, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and legislation. 10/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 | 補充活動 | 類別 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 目標 21 | 33. 透過針對性的能力建構，以及針對全面性生物多樣性監測與創新技術（包括數位技術、遙測及國家生物多樣性資料庫）之開發，強化生物多樣性監測、資料管理與知識分享進展之應用，以改善監測、評估、報告與決策 [關於生物多樣性成果、生態連結性與代表性，以及] 涉及 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 之事項，包括透過國家適切之方法與指標，同時強化管理與整合生物多樣性資料之能力與基礎設施。 | B |\n| 目標 22 | 34. 強化原住民族與地方社區在決策中取得資訊之管道，以及完整、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應之代表性與參與 [與保護區及保育共生地相關，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 35. [確保] 原住民族與地方社區、女性、兒童、青年及身心障礙者能依據國家立法及其他相關國際協議，獲得司法救濟[，包括透過建立有效且易於取得的申訴機制，]以處理與建立、管理及治理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 相關之議題。 36. [確保] 全面保護從事與 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 相關活動之環境人權捍衛者。 | B |\n| 目標 23 | 37. 促進性別平等並整合性別回應之方法，包括使用 [按性別分類之指標][性別分層指標]，貫穿整個工作計畫[，並適當考慮性別暴力]。 | A |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">補充活動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">類別</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 21</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">33. 透過針對性的能力建構，以及針對全面性生物多樣性監測與創新技術（包括數位技術、遙測及國家生物多樣性資料庫）之開發，強化生物多樣性監測、資料管理與知識分享進展之應用，以改善監測、評估、報告與決策 [關於生物多樣性成果、生態連結性與代表性，以及] 涉及 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地，] 之事項，包括透過國家適切之方法與指標，同時強化管理與整合生物多樣性資料之能力與基礎設施。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 22</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">34. 強化原住民族與地方社區在決策中取得資訊之管道，以及完整、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應之代表性與參與 [與保護區及保育共生地相關，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地]。 35. [確保] 原住民族與地方社區、女性、兒童、青年及身心障礙者能依據國家立法及其他相關國際協議，獲得司法救濟[，包括透過建立有效且易於取得的申訴機制，]以處理與建立、管理及治理 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 相關之議題。 36. [確保] 全面保護從事與 [保護區與保育共生地，在適用情況下，認可原住民族與傳統領地] 相關活動之環境人權捍衛者。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">目標 23</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">37. 促進性別平等並整合性別回應之方法，包括使用 [按性別分類之指標][性別分層指標]，貫穿整個工作計畫[，並適當考慮性別暴力]。</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">A</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"[II.","html":"<p>[II.</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]},{"md":"計畫要素 5：生態連結性","html":"<p>計畫要素 5：生態連結性</p>","en":[18,19]},{"md":"目標\n3.\n維持、增強並復育陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之結構性與功能性生態連結性，包括透過將具生態代表性且連結良好之系統[（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）之保護區與保育共生地]，整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景中。","html":"<p>目標<br />\n3.<br />\n維持、增強並復育陸域、內陸水域、沿岸及海洋生態系之結構性與功能性生態連結性，包括透過將具生態代表性且連結良好之系統[（在適用情況下，承認原住民族與傳統領地）之保護區與保育共生地]，整合至更廣泛的景觀與海景中。</p>","en":[20,21]},{"md":"長期目標 5.1 – 整合規劃與執行\n4.\n根據國家情況、優先事項與立法，將生態網絡、生態廊道、踏腳石及其他維持、增強或復育生態連結性之措施，整合至具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃、生態系復育、氣候變遷調適以及相關部門與基礎設施規劃中。","html":"<p>長期目標 5.1 – 整合規劃與執行<br />\n4.<br />\n根據國家情況、優先事項與立法，將生態網絡、生態廊道、踏腳石及其他維持、增強或復育生態連結性之措施，整合至具生物多樣性包容性的空間規劃、生態系復育、氣候變遷調適以及相關部門與基礎設施規劃中。</p>","en":[22,23]}],"csv":[{"f":"non-paper-item-17-c/p005-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad63c4345af13551e4801d5/p011.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 17 (c) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"Goal 5.2 – Equitable governance and enabling conditions"},{"t":"5. Promote equitable and effective governance, the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, the recognition and respect for their rights, including over their traditional territories, and the application of free, prior and informed consent,13 as applicable, while strengthening financial resources, capacity-building and development, technical and scientific cooperation and access to and transfer of technology."},{"t":"Goal 5.3 – Cooperation and coordination"},{"t":"6. Strengthen, as appropriate, national, transboundary and cross-sectoral cooperation on ecological connectivity and promote synergies with the Convention on the Conservation of Migratory Species of Wild Animals14 and other relevant multilateral environmental agreements and initiatives, in accordance with their respective mandates and while avoiding duplication. Goal 5.4 – Monitoring and knowledge"},{"t":"7. Strengthen nationally appropriate approaches and indicators for monitoring structural and functional ecological connectivity, drawing on scientific information and indigenous and local knowledge, subject to free, prior and informed consent, as applicable, and taking into account relevant findings of the methodological assessment of integrated biodiversity-inclusive spatial planning and ecological connectivity of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services once approved by the Plenary of the Platform.] __________"},{"t":"13 “Free, prior and informed consent” refers to the tripartite terminology of “prior and informed consent”, “free, prior and"},{"t":"informed consent” and “approval and involvement”."},{"t":"14 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1651, No. 28395."},{"t":"11/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 17 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"長期目標 5.2 – 公平治理與促成條件\n5.\n促進公平且有效的治理、原住民族與地方社區的全面且有效參與、對其權利（包括對其傳統領地的權利）的承認與尊重，並在適用情況下落實自由、事先及知情同意，¹³ 同時強化財務資源、能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作，以及技術的取得與轉移。","html":"<p>長期目標 5.2 – 公平治理與促成條件<br />\n5.<br />\n促進公平且有效的治理、原住民族與地方社區的全面且有效參與、對其權利（包括對其傳統領地的權利）的承認與尊重，並在適用情況下落實自由、事先及知情同意，¹³ 同時強化財務資源、能力建構與發展、技術與科學合作，以及技術的取得與轉移。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"長期目標 5.3 – 合作與協調\n6.\n視適當情況，強化關於生態連結性的國家、跨境及跨部門合作，並根據各自的職權，在避免重複的情況下，促進與《保護遷徙野生動物公約》¹⁴ 及其他相關多邊環境協議與倡議之間的綜效。","html":"<p>長期目標 5.3 – 合作與協調<br />\n6.<br />\n視適當情況，強化關於生態連結性的國家、跨境及跨部門合作，並根據各自的職權，在避免重複的情況下，促進與《保護遷徙野生動物公約》¹⁴ 及其他相關多邊環境協議與倡議之間的綜效。</p>","en":[3,4]},{"md":"長期目標 5.4 – 監測與知識\n7.\n強化用於監測結構性與功能性生態連結性的國家適當方法與指標，並利用科學資訊以及在適用情況下符合自由、事先及知情同意原則的原住民族與地方知識，並考量「生物多樣性與生態系服務之政府間科學－政策平台」針對整合性生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估相關結果（一旦經該平台全體會議批准）。]\n__________","html":"<p>長期目標 5.4 – 監測與知識<br />\n7.<br />\n強化用於監測結構性與功能性生態連結性的國家適當方法與指標，並利用科學資訊以及在適用情況下符合自由、事先及知情同意原則的原住民族與地方知識，並考量「生物多樣性與生態系服務之政府間科學－政策平台」針對整合性生物多樣性包容性空間規劃與生態連結性之方法論評估相關結果（一旦經該平台全體會議批准）。]</p>\n<hr />","en":[5]},{"md":"¹³ 「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。\n¹⁴ 聯合國，條約集，第 1651 卷，第 28395 號。","html":"<p>¹³ 「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。<br />\n¹⁴ 聯合國，條約集，第 1651 卷，第 28395 號。</p>","en":[6,7,8,9]}]}]};
